295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 125 0 R
/T (First, this happens because skills are not captured during project execution. Coditas confirms that documentation primarily occurs at the beginning and end of projects, leaving a critical gap during execution where most learning takes place. As a result, newly acquired skills are not transformed into organizational knowledge and remain invisible beyond the immediate project context.  Second, skills are not effectively maintained, as the current process relies on manual input from engineers. The  BPMN shows that engineers are required to update their skills through forms, but this step is often skipped.  Specifically, Coditas has attempted such approaches, but adoption was low due to time constraints and competing  projects priorities. Research supports this behaviour, efficiency and value delivery got prioritised first, and non- essential tasks such as manual updates are often avoided in value stream management \(Takakura n.d.\). )
/E (First, this happens because skills are not captured during project execution. Coditas confirms that documentation primarily occurs at the beginning and end of projects, leaving a critical gap during execution where most learning takes place. As a result, newly acquired skills are not transformed into organizational knowledge and remain invisible beyond the immediate project context.  Second, skills are not effectively maintained, as the current process relies on manual input from engineers. The  BPMN shows that engineers are required to update their skills through forms, but this step is often skipped.  Specifically, Coditas has attempted such approaches, but adoption was low due to time constraints and competing  projects priorities. Research supports this behaviour, efficiency and value delivery got prioritised first, and non- essential tasks such as manual updates are often avoided in value stream management \(Takakura n.d.\). )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
