1359 0 obj
<<
/Title (Another negative implication is that Coditas is more likely to not hire the best possible engineers based on the requirements of their projects. In such situations, engineers may not have the proper skills and abilities to deliver a specific job effectively.  As a result, it will take longer for them to get started because they would have to learn how to use the required tools.  It can also lead to lower quality due to higher operational errors \(Vantighem 2026\).  At the same time, some employees who would be better for particular jobs are less visible to other Coditas managers.  This means that the organization may miss out on the utilization of those talents. Our analysis suggests that Coditas  can potentially loses $357,955 per year because of ineffective staffing \(Appendix A\).)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1344 0 R
/Prev 1364 0 R
/Next 1355 0 R
>>
